---
const events = [
  { t: "0", state: "On" },
  { t: "1", state: "Off" },
  { t: "1½", state: "On" },
  { t: "1¾", state: "Off" },
  { t: "1⅞", state: "On" },
  { t: "2", state: "Not specified" },
]
---

<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">The lamp switches infinitely often before two minutes have passed.</p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-center text-base sm:grid-cols-6">
    {events.map((ev, i) => (
      <div class="border-2 border-ink p-2">
        <p class="font-bold">{ev.t} min</p>
        <p class={i === 5 ? "text-accent font-bold" : "font-normal"}>{ev.state}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <svg
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm"
    viewBox="0 0 300 92"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="lamp-title lamp-desc"
  >
    <title id="lamp-title">Switching events gather closer to the two-minute mark</title>
    <desc id="lamp-desc">
      At one minute, one and a half, one and three quarters, and so forth, the switch intervals
      halve and crowd toward two minutes.
    </desc>
    <path d="M14 50 H286" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
    {[14, 150, 218, 252, 269, 286].map((x, i) => (
      <g>
        <circle cx={x} cy="50" r="5" fill={i === 5 ? "#bd4b37" : "#387a91"} />
      </g>
    ))}
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16">
      <text x="14" y="30" text-anchor="middle">
        0
      </text>
      <text x="150" y="30" text-anchor="middle">
        1
      </text>
      <text x="294" y="30" text-anchor="end">
        2 min
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="82">
        Half the remaining wait every time
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    The rules say what happens at each switching time <em>before</em> minute two. There is no
    last switch. The story does not specify a state at exactly two minutes, so neither “on” nor
    “off” is forced by the alternating pattern.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
